<title>BELGIUM: TABLE - Solvay H1 1997 net profit flat.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Solvay H1 1997 net profit flat.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1997</p>
<p>(in billions of francs, unless stated)</p>
<p>    Cons net profit		 6.1  vs   6.0</p>
<p>    Cons net/share (francs)     692  vs   690</p>
<p>    Cons current profit	   6.1  vs   5.9</p>
<p>    Cons current/share (francs) 692  vs   672</p>
<p>    Extraordinary items	   zero vs   0.1</p>
<p>    Sales			   153.8  vs 142.2</p>
<p>    Cash flow			16.3  vs  15.7</p>
<p>NOTE - Solvay is a Belgian chemicals group. Analysts had expected flat to slightly firmer earnings.  </p>
<p>    EBIT *			   10.6  vs  11.0</p>
<p>    Net debt expense		1.2  vs   1.7</p>
<p>    Taxes			     3.3  vs   3.4</p>
<p>NOTE - * earnings before interest (net debt expense), taxes, and unallocated items per sector.</p>
<p>EBIT by sector (in billion bfr):</p>
<p>    chemicals			 3.7  vs   6.1</p>
<p>    plastics			  3.6  vs   1.6</p>
<p>    processing			1.3  vs   1.3</p>
<p>    health			    2.0  vs   3.7</p>
<p>Sales by sector (in billion bfr):</p>
<p>    chemicals			49.2  vs  49.1</p>
<p>    plastics			 55.2  vs  42.2</p>
<p>    processing		     29.3  vs  27.8</p>
<p>    health			   20.1  vs  41.1</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
</text>
